                ["VerHist_Title"] = "Version History",
                ["VerHist_Subtitle"] = "Summary overview - for the full, detailed history of every change, see the project's HANDOFF.md file.",
                ["VerHist_510Title"] = "v5.1.0 - WSL2 manager, RGB conflict detector, winget pin/export/import, and more",
                ["VerHist_510Desc"] = "New: a WSL2 manager - list your Linux distributions, open a shell, set the default, terminate or fully unregister one, update WSL, or shut everything down, right from the app. New: an RGB conflict detector that flags when two or more RGB lighting control programs from different vendors (e.g. Corsair iCUE + ASUS Aura Sync) are running at the same time, a common cause of flickering. The Software Update Manager now supports winget pin, so you can lock an app out of future upgrades, plus export/import of your installed app list to move it to another computer.",
                ["VerHist_520Title"] = "v5.2.0 - Tab merges, FPS/Widget fix, MIT+GPL3 license, and more",
                ["VerHist_520Desc"] = "The software update card in Optimization now has a large circular, animated scan button (like the driver one) instead of a plain button - the old update shortcuts were removed from Home. The disk health trend moved to the end of the Health & Maintenance tab. Windows built-in components and Windows optional features were unified into one card (Apps & Bloat tab), as was duplicate file finding with the storage tools (System tab). Version History is now a tab inside the Help window - its sidebar shortcut was replaced with Clipboard History. The Menu and Language tabs in Appearance Settings were merged into one. Fixed a bug that permanently prevented FPS from showing in the Desktop/Gaming Widget. The Microsoft PC Manager/Windows Classic skins were removed from the theme dropdown - they're now selectable only from the Skins tab. The License now also includes the full text of the GNU GPL v3.0.",
                ["VerHist_530Title"] = "v5.3.0 - New Name: GearWin - Complete PC Care",
                ["VerHist_530Desc"] = "The app was renamed to \"GearWin\" with the subtitle \"Complete PC Care\" (after checking app-store listings and trademark registries to avoid colliding with existing products) - the executable, window titles, tray icon, installer, and license were all updated to match. The code's internal namespace and the user data folder stay the same, so no existing settings are lost in this update.",
                ["VerHist_4100Title"] = "v4.10.0 - Password breach check, system image backup, unified profile manager, and more",
                ["VerHist_4100Desc"] = "New: check whether a password has appeared in known data breaches, using the Have I Been Pwned database with full privacy (only a partial hash leaves this computer). New: one-click system image backup using Windows' built-in backup tool, onto a separate target drive. The profile manager (named profiles + file export/import) is now unified into a single card instead of two separate ones. Disk health detection now also reliably covers NVMe drives, not just SATA. The battery card now links directly to Windows' per-app battery usage breakdown.",
                ["VerHist_490Title"] = "v4.9.0 - Clipboard manager, folder encryption, GPU/FPS game overlay, and more",
                ["VerHist_490Desc"] = "Big feature round: a searchable Clipboard History (Win+Shift+V, or from the tray) with local, unencrypted storage - clear anytime. Folder Lock encrypts any folder into a single password-protected file (AES-256, works on every Windows edition) and securely erases the original. The Desktop Widget is now the Performance & Game Widget - it also shows GPU usage and an estimated FPS during fullscreen games. Home now has a small Updates snapshot (drivers/apps) so you don't need to check three separate places. BitLocker recovery keys and USB device history are now viewable from inside the app, and Network & Security now warns you if DNS-over-HTTPS is silently bypassing the telemetry-blocking hosts file.",
                ["VerHist_482Title"] = "v4.8.2 - Fixed: several UI elements stayed in the old language until restart",
                ["VerHist_482Desc"] = "Changing the app's language while it's running now updates everything live, without needing to close and reopen it: the system tray icon's menu (it's WinForms, outside WPF's normal binding system), the horizontal menu strip's shortcuts (the sidebar's alternate layout), and the status bar's idle text now all refresh immediately. Also fixed the theme toggle button (Light/Dark Mode) - it was hardcoded in English and never went through the translation system at all, regardless of language.",
                ["VerHist_481Title"] = "v4.8.1 - Fixed: Version History window was still stuck on old entries",
                ["VerHist_481Desc"] = "The in-app Version History window used a fully static, hardcoded list of entries instead of reflecting the current release's changelog - so the last two updates (Arabic RTL/caching fixes, and the Arabic & Hindi language addition) never actually appeared there, even though the underlying text already existed. Fixed by wiring both entries in; the window now reflects the real, current version.",
                ["VerHist_480Title"] = "v4.8.0 - Arabic RTL layout, faster tab switching, UI fixes",
                ["VerHist_480Desc"] = "Arabic now renders with a proper right-to-left layout (not just translated text) across the main window and all secondary windows/dialogs. The Recommended Apps installed-check and the My Device hardware scan no longer re-run on every single tab visit - both are cached for the session, with an explicit Refresh button for when something changed outside the app. Fixed: the common-feature shortcut chips in Additional Windows Features were too small (missing font size); the Check Updates via Microsoft Store button is now on the same row as Scan/Upgrade Selected instead of its own line. Also documented silent/unattended installer flags (/VERYSILENT) in the README.",
                ["VerHist_470Title"] = "v4.7.0 - Arabic & Hindi (14 languages total), richer tray menu, license disclosure",
                ["VerHist_470Desc"] = "Added two new languages - Arabic and Hindi - bringing the total to 14 fully translated languages. The system tray icon's menu now also offers Quick Clean and Health Check shortcuts, plus a checkable Desktop Widget toggle, without opening the main window. Two new keyboard shortcuts: Ctrl+F focuses the search box, Ctrl+H opens the Full Health Check directly. The License tab (and installer) now properly discloses the bundled third-party libraries (LibreHardwareMonitorLib under MPL 2.0, PDFsharp under MIT).",
                ["VerHist_460Title"] = "v4.6.0 - Disk Health on Home, Named Profiles, Desktop Widget",
                ["VerHist_460Desc"] = "Home now shows a S.M.A.R.T. disk health badge next to the Health Score. New \"Named Profiles\" (Extra Settings tab) - save your full settings (theme, tweaks, language, sidebar) under a name and switch between them instantly, alongside the existing file-based Export/Import. New \"Desktop Widget\" (Appearance Settings) - an always-visible, draggable CPU/RAM/Network widget on your desktop, separate from the click-to-open tray popup. Also several performance and reliability improvements under the hood: parallel duplicate-file hashing, parallel health checks, a 24h cache for driver-catalog scans, fuzzy search matching, queued toast notifications, and auto-detected system language on first launch.",
                ["VerHist_450Title"] = "v4.5.0 - All 12 Languages Complete, Windows Classic Skin Fixes",
                ["VerHist_450Desc"] = "The app is now fully translated into all 12 languages (Greek, English, German, French, Spanish, Italian, Russian, Chinese, Japanese, Portuguese, Korean, Turkish) - the quick language picker on the main window now offers all of them too. Fixed the Windows Classic skin: menu dropdowns, the ComboBox dropdown, and the main window's quick pickers now correctly use square corners instead of staying rounded; three secondary dialog windows (Add Right-Click Option, Further Analysis, Health Check) that were missing the skin's square window corners now get them too.",
                ["VerHist_444Title"] = "v4.4.4 - Duplicate Finder, Open Ports, Tray Widget & Full Profile",
                ["VerHist_444Desc"] = "New \"Duplicate File Finder\" (Advanced Tools) - pick a folder, finds files with exactly the same content (size + hash). New \"Open Ports\" (Network & Security) - shows which TCP ports are listening and which process owns them. The app now has a system tray icon with a mini popup (CPU/RAM/Network) so you don't need to open the main window. Export/Import Profile (Extra Settings) now covers your ENTIRE experience (theme, language, sidebar, pinned shortcuts), not just tweaks. Also fixed a real bug that stopped the Scheduled Tasks scan (same root cause as a previous fix: PowerShell doesn't always serialize an enum as text).",
                ["VerHist_443Title"] = "v4.4.3 - Expanded Registry Cleaner, Backup History & Check Reminder",
                ["VerHist_443Desc"] = "The Registry Cleaner now also scans for orphaned Shared DLLs. A new \"Registry Backup History\" (Health & Maintenance) shows and restores the automatic .reg backups from every deletion - previously only reachable manually outside the app. The extra health-findings card in the Full Health Check now has a button that jumps straight to the System tab. Startup apps now show Low/Medium/High impact based on their real measured delay. Home gently reminds you if it's been 7+ days since your last Full Health Check.",
                ["VerHist_442Title"] = "v4.4.2 - Fix: Result Tiles Now Refresh After Optimizing",
                ["VerHist_442Desc"] = "A user reported that after clicking \"Optimize Now\" in the Full Health Check, the result tiles kept showing the OLD numbers (e.g. still saying \"19 registry entries\" even though the actual cleanup HAD happened - confirmed with a real test finding that deletion works correctly). Now, after cleaning, the stages that were cleaned are automatically rescanned and every tile updates with fresh results. Also, if registry cleanup genuinely fails (e.g. without Administrator rights), the app now reports it honestly instead of falsely claiming success.",
                ["VerHist_441Title"] = "v4.4.1 - Unified Full Health Check & Icon Consistency",
                ["VerHist_441Desc"] = "Quick Clean and Full Health Check were merged into ONE entry point (the duplicate Home card was removed). Full Health Check now shows a real 0-100 score in its results, exports a PDF report, and also scans browser cache alongside disk space. The \"Usage Traces\" stage was explicitly renamed to \"Registry Cleanup\" and its scan was expanded (App Paths, orphaned startup entries). The last remaining emoji icons (in Help window tab headers and 9 cards elsewhere in the app) were replaced with the same vector icon system, and their gentle pulse was strengthened to be clearly visible.",
                ["VerHist_440Title"] = "v4.4.0 - Complete User Guide with Animated Icons",
                ["VerHist_440Desc"] = "Help was completely rewritten - from 8 short general paragraphs (one per tab) to a detailed explanation of EVERY function and button, organized per tab and per card (53 separate write-ups), each with the real, animated (gentle pulse) icon of that feature - the same icon system the app already uses, not new, unrelated icons.",
                ["VerHist_437Title"] = "v4.3.7 - PDF Export, Distinct Toggles & Chips",
                ["VerHist_437Desc"] = "The \"My Device\" export now produces a real PDF file instead of a .txt (new PdfExportService, PDFsharp). Fixes found during live Light Mode testing: the toggle switches in the Windows Optional Features list were nearly invisible in light themes (a white circle on an almost-white background) - a visible outline was added everywhere. The blue popular-feature chips were too cramped, with text not fitting comfortably - more padding.",
                ["VerHist_436Title"] = "v4.3.6 - Fixes Found During Live Testing",
                ["VerHist_436Desc"] = "The \"Application Uninstall\" pill in the Full Health Check was clipped at the window's edge - the window is now wider. Real bug: refreshing Windows Optional Features could crash the entire scan with \"The requested operation requires an element of type 'String', but the target element has type 'Number'\" whenever PowerShell returned a feature's state as a number instead of text - fixed to recognize both forms, so the whole list no longer fails because of one feature.",
                ["VerHist_435Title"] = "v4.3.5 - Network Traffic Per App, Faster Startup & Many Fixes",
                ["VerHist_435Desc"] = "New: network traffic per app (Network & Security, via ETW), 40+ new unit tests (13 to 54), faster startup (CPU/GPU counter initialization moved to a background thread, no longer delays the main window's first paint), progress bars no longer get stuck on an exception (Winget update check/Driver Store/Full Health Check - the latter with a new \"Retry\" button on stage failure). Fixes found during live testing: the Full Health Check graphic no longer gets clipped in the window and each stage now stays visibly lit for at least a moment, invisible Quick Clean text in dark theme, overlapping \"Pinned\"/\"Disk Analysis\" cards on Home, a cramped Microsoft Store button, tiny buttons in Lighter Windows, indistinct popular-feature chips, and a real bug where refreshing Windows Optional Features always said \"run as Administrator\" (even when the app was already elevated) instead of the real, encoding-mangled PowerShell error message.",
                ["VerHist_430Title"] = "v4.3.0 - Toasts, File Shredder, Autologon & More",
                ["VerHist_430Desc"] = "New: toast notifications for key events (Quick Clean, Battery Report, Diagnostics .zip), \"AI-style\" delete-safety scoring per file (age + file type, not real ML) with a secure File Shredder (3-pass random overwrite - note: not guaranteed on SSD/NVMe due to wear-leveling), an Autologon helper with an explicit plain-text password storage warning, popular Windows Features shortcuts, lazy tab loading, virtualized lists for processes/services/scheduled tasks/firewall rules, smooth progress bar animation, card hover elevation, a pulsing red health-attention dot when the score is low, and smarter refresh throttling when the app is in the background. Fixed 2 real bugs where Find Large Files/Duplicates could crash on an access-denied folder (e.g. \"My Music\").",
                ["VerHist_410Title"] = "v4.1.0 - New Name, Quick Clean & PC Manager-Style Health Check",
                ["VerHist_410Desc"] = "The app was renamed to \"PC Performance & Maintenance Suite\" (a legal check confirmed the previous name violated Microsoft's naming rule). New: Quick Clean on Home (8 categories beyond temp files, with an animated broom during scanning), a full Health Check in a secondary window (PC Manager style, with real data from each scan), pinned tweak shortcuts on Home, a performance history sparkline on every tile, per-app startup delay estimates, tweak profile export/import, dedicated SSD/NVMe tile icons, flags in the language menu, and README screenshots. Fixed a real bug where Quick Clean could hang forever on an access-denied folder.",
                ["VerHist_400Title"] = "v4.0.0 - Scheduled Maintenance, Boot Timeline, S.M.A.R.T. & Much More",
                ["VerHist_400Desc"] = "New: Weekly scheduled maintenance (Task Scheduler), Automatic Gaming Mode, Boot Timeline, real S.M.A.R.T. disk health checking with a trend over time (fixed a bug where it was always hardcoded to \"Healthy\"), third-party Scheduled Tasks viewer, per-process memory usage history. Also: Quick DNS Switch, Public Wi-Fi Detection, Battery Report, Diagnostic .zip Report, bulk app installs per category, bloatware/startup cross-reference, \"My Device\" export, outdated driver flagging, a new \"What the app did recently\" card, search in Tweaks, ReadyToRun for faster startup. Full audit of the status bar/progress bars across the whole app, CONTRIBUTING.md/CHANGELOG.md.",
                ["VerHist_370Title"] = "v3.7.0 - Vector Icons & Visual Fixes",
                ["VerHist_370Desc"] = "Every emoji in the app (card titles, tabs, sidebar, onboarding guide) was replaced with new vector icons that correctly follow every theme/mode. Fixed the \"Orbit\" animated background (now elliptical, angled, and strictly clipped to the tab strip). Fixed a \"C::\" typo in storage drives. New \"System Information\" header.",
                ["VerHist_360Title"] = "v3.6.0 - Lighter App, Lighter Windows & Visual Additions",
                ["VerHist_360Desc"] = "New \"Lighter Windows\" card in Tweaks (disable Background Apps, SysMain/Superfetch, Indexing Options, Low Resource Usage Profile). \"My Device\" now caches data that doesn't change within a session. The animated background also pauses when the window becomes invisible, not just on minimize. Smoother tab transitions, a red attention dot on the Health tab when the score is low, and a before/after free-space comparison after clearing browser cache. Honesty note: colored rendering of the tutorial icons was tried with two different font fixes, neither fully worked in this environment - still open, needs real vector icons.",
                ["VerHist_351Title"] = "v3.5.1 - Visual Fixes: Header Spacing, App Theme, Thermometers",
                ["VerHist_351Desc"] = "More breathing room between the tab strip and the title, with more of the animated background visible. Fixed a real bug that made the \"App Theme\" ComboBox appear light-colored in ALL themes (dark and light) instead of the actual theme color - verified with a live pixel measurement. Temperature icons (🌡) were replaced with vector icons, correctly colored on every Windows version.",
                ["VerHist_350Title"] = "v3.5.0 - Four Known Gaps Fixed",
                ["VerHist_350Desc"] = "Toggles in Tweaks now show the real current registry state (verified live) instead of always starting off. The restore point before installing a driver (Microsoft Update Catalog) is now automatic, not a separate question. Fixed a real bug in the Windows Defender detection on \"My Device\" (wrong WMI class name). The \"Skins\" tab now goes through the translation system.",
                ["VerHist_344Title"] = "v3.4.4 - Installer Update Detection Fix",
                ["VerHist_344Desc"] = "The “existing installation detected” message on the installer's welcome page never showed up due to an incorrectly formatted registry path - fixed, verified the registry key now reads correctly.",
                ["VerHist_343Title"] = "v3.4.3 - First-Run Crash Fix",
                ["VerHist_343Desc"] = "In some cases, closing the tutorial on the app's first launch (Skip/Get Started) caused a “Cannot set Owner property” error because it was momentarily the only open window - fixed, verified live.",
                ["VerHist_342Title"] = "v3.4.2 - Smart Update & Richer Tutorial",
                ["VerHist_342Desc"] = "The installer now detects an existing installation and copies only the files that actually changed instead of the whole app, with a matching message on the welcome page. The first-run tutorial was rewritten so every page explains concrete features and how to use them (which buttons to press), not just a general description of each tab.",
                ["VerHist_341Title"] = "v3.4.1 - Tutorial Button Visibility Fix",
                ["VerHist_341Desc"] = "The “View Tutorial” button in Help had very low contrast in some themes and looked like plain text instead of a button - it now uses a solid accent color, clearly visible in every theme.",
                ["VerHist_340Title"] = "v3.4.0 - First-Run Tutorial & Safer Uninstall",
                ["VerHist_340Desc"] = "A new illustrated tutorial appears on the app's first launch (10 slides, one per tab), and can be replayed anytime from Help. The installer now asks at uninstall time whether to restore all Windows settings the app changed back to their real previous values, and an app description page was added to the setup wizard.",
                ["VerHist_330Title"] = "v3.3.0 - My Device & More Accurate Disk Detection",
                ["VerHist_330Desc"] = "New \"My Device\" section at the top of the System tab - 8 cards with full hardware/OS details (Motherboard, Drives, OS, Network, CPU, Battery, RAM, GPU), purely informational, no buttons. Fixed a bug that made disk type detection (NVMe/SATA/USB) fail on certain disks due to a Storage WMI provider limitation - replaced with a reliable, verified method. Also added a correct local administrators count.",
                ["VerHist_321Title"] = "v3.2.1 - Network Status on Home",
                ["VerHist_321Desc"] = "New connection status indicator (🟢 Connected / 🔴 No Internet, with latency in ms) on the Home tab, plus a live network traffic graph (like Task Manager) and a quick-jump button to Network & Security.",
                ["VerHist_320Title"] = "v3.2.0 - Telemetry Blocking, Cloud Cleanup & Memory Freeing",
                ["VerHist_320Desc"] = "New \"Privacy & Protection\" card in Network & Security, with blocking of known Microsoft telemetry endpoints (hosts file, reversible). New large-file finder tools for local Google Drive/Dropbox folders (when detected). New \"Free Memory\" button in System - frees up idle memory used by background apps without closing them.",
                ["VerHist_311Title"] = "v3.1.1 - Lighter app, cleaner animated background",
                ["VerHist_311Desc"] = "The animated background is now confined to the title/tab-strip area (no longer hidden behind content cards) and removed entirely from secondary windows (Help, Version History, Appearance Settings, etc.). It now pauses automatically when the app is minimized or unfocused - idle CPU usage dropped by ~80%. Increased contrast on several background styles (Gears, Orbit, Waves, etc.) that were too faint, especially in Light mode. Fixed the Greek flag in the language picker (it showed the wrong design).",
                ["VerHist_310Title"] = "v3.1.0 - Full translation, visual & temperature fixes",
                ["VerHist_310Desc"] = "The entire app is now translated into 4 languages (Greek/English/German/French), including every status/confirmation/error message and every secondary window. SDIO driver updates no longer download/install automatically - scan only. Added real GPU/Disk icons on the Home tab and larger icons on all hardware tiles. The animated title gear now reproduces the exact 2.8.2 layout, with bigger, more legible teeth. Fixed: a false 0°C CPU temperature reading (now correctly shows 🔒 when VBS blocks access), poor status-bar contrast on 3 themes, a malformed dropdown in the disk benchmark, cramped buttons in Health Tools, a missing VLC icon, a wrong Viber winget ID, and the Additional Windows Features refresh button silently failing instead of showing an error. The side menu now sizes to its actual content instead of stretching, and the main window is more compact.",
                ["VerHist_300Title"] = "v3.0.0 - New release: full move to WPF",
                ["VerHist_300Desc"] = "The app was rebuilt from scratch on modern technology (.NET 8/WPF instead of WinForms) - faster, smoother, with real window resizing. All 8 tabs are fully functional. Driver Updates became multi-source, unified into ONE list: Windows Update, Microsoft Update Catalog, AMD/NVIDIA (official pages), Dell Command Update and Snappy Driver Installer (always silent, no window of its own) - flagged '✓✓ Confirmed' when two independent sources agree. Added real app logos (downloaded once, cached locally), a grouped recommended-apps list, a unified list of optional Windows features, a full Win11 toggle panel in ViVeTool, a new Appearance Settings window with live preview, and dozens of visual/stability fixes.",
                ["VerHist_278Title"] = "2.7 – 2.8.2 · Real resizing & final polish",
                ["VerHist_278Desc"] = "The window gained real resize/maximize support, with proportional content scaling. Scrollbars were fully themed, the status bar grew larger, an 'Installed App Management' feature was added, and a false 'restart pending' indicator in the Health Score was fixed.",
                ["VerHist_26Title"] = "2.1 – 2.6 · Embedded menu & multi-source driver updates",
                ["VerHist_26Desc"] = "The side menu became truly embedded in the main window. Driver scanning expanded to multiple official sources (Windows Update, AMD, NVIDIA, Dell) with a 'Confirmed' flag when two sources agree. Added Lenovo/HP computer detection, subtle toast notifications, and the 'Microsoft PC Manager' appearance theme.",
                ["VerHist_20Title"] = "2.0 · New Home tab & a host of tools",
                ["VerHist_20Desc"] = "Added the 'Home' tab with CPU/Memory/Disk meters, a System Health Score with auto-fix, Disk Space Analysis by category, a Defender Quick Scan and Browser Cache Cleanup. Also added a full list of Windows Features, Deep Uninstall, Ghost Device Management, Custom Right-Click Options, and a Hosts file editor.",
                ["VerHist_19Title"] = "1.8 – 1.9 · Drivers, Health & Security",
                ["VerHist_19Desc"] = "Added the first Device Driver Update (Windows Update), new system health checks, and an 'AI & Copilot' section. Followed by System Restore Points, Firewall Rules Management, global search, Services optimization, Action History, driver backups, and a safe Registry Cleaner.",
                ["VerHist_17Title"] = "1.7 · Stabilization & organization",
                ["VerHist_17Desc"] = "Recommended Apps were organized into 7 clear categories, buttons gained richer themed effects, and new Windows 11-style toggles were added. Translation of the entire Version History into 4 languages was completed.",
                ["VerHist_16Title"] = "1.6 · Themes and animated backgrounds",
                ["VerHist_16Desc"] = "Appearance themes gained an authentic period style (Windows 98, Vista/Aero, Nordic/Solarized) and selectable animated backgrounds (Gears, Orbits, Particles). Appearance Settings were reorganized into tabs with live preview.",
                ["VerHist_15Title"] = "1.4 – 1.5 · Modern menu and first translations",
                ["VerHist_15Desc"] = "Added the Version History, a new optional modern menu (sidebar or horizontal), and the Recommended Apps category (K-Lite, 7-Zip, VLC, PowerToys, etc). Support for English/French/German began.",
                ["VerHist_13Title"] = "1.0 – 1.3 · The foundations",
                ["VerHist_13Desc"] = "The app started as a simple tabless window with a basic dark theme. It gained a tab structure (Optimization, Health, Network, Tools), automatic Administrator elevation, the first appearance themes (light/dark), and vector icons. Added ViVeTool for experimental Windows features, the K-Lite codec pack, safe uninstall of Metro/UWP apps, and high-DPI display support.",
                ["Help_Title"] = "Help & Information",
                ["Help_InstructionsTab"] = "Instructions",
                ["Help_Shortcuts"] = "Ctrl+1 through Ctrl+8: quick tab switching. Ctrl+M: show/hide the classic menu. Ctrl+F: focus the search box. Ctrl+H: open the Full Health Check. The search box at the top shows live results from all tabs/tools/settings as you type.",
                ["Help_HomeTitle"] = "Home",
                ["Help_HomeDesc"] = "Real-time CPU/RAM/Disk/Temperature meters (temperatures only show if Memory Integrity/VBS isn't blocking direct hardware access - 🔒 instead of a value means this). System Health Score with auto-fix for findings. Disk Space Analysis by category with drill-down.",
                ["Help_Home_Monitoring"] = "The CPU/RAM/GPU/Disk bars update every 1 second. The ‹ › arrows on the disk tile cycle through all your connected drives.",
                ["Help_Home_NetworkStatusTitle"] = "Network Status",
                ["Help_Home_NetworkStatus"] = "The green/red dot shows whether there's real Internet access (ping, not just a local cable/Wi-Fi link), with a live traffic graph next to it. The \"Network & Security\" button jumps straight to that tab.",
                ["Help_Home_HealthScore"] = "A 0-100 score with a findings list. \"Fix All\" automatically fixes ONLY storage findings (clears %TEMP%) - Windows Defender findings are only surfaced, never changed automatically. \"Refresh\" recomputes the score. \"Full Health Check\" opens the graphical, step-by-step tool (PC Manager style) in its own window - it also covers quick disk/browser-cache cleanup, registry, settings, apps, and network in one unified flow.",
                ["Help_Home_Pinned"] = "Shows the tweaks you've pinned (★) from Additional Settings, with a direct on/off switch, no tab switching needed.",
                ["Help_Home_DiskAnalysis"] = "\"Analyze\" builds one colored bar with the real size of each category (Games/Apps/Photos/Videos/Documents/Downloads/Windows/Other). Clicking a segment or a legend entry opens a detailed folder drill-down for that category (except \"Other\").",
                ["Help_Home_RecentActivity"] = "Shows the 3 most recent app actions in real time. \"See All\" opens the full Action History in its own window.",
                ["Help_OptTitle"] = "Optimization",
                ["Help_OptDesc"] = "Office Mode / Gaming Mode (power profile + settings). Multi-source Driver Update merged into ONE list - Windows Update, Microsoft Update Catalog, official AMD/NVIDIA pages, Dell Command Update, Snappy Driver Installer (always silent), and Lenovo detection - flagged '✓✓ Confirmed' when two independent sources agree. Driver backup/restore, driver store cleanup, and the Software Update Manager (winget + Microsoft Store).",
                ["Help_Opt_OfficeMode"] = "The switch applies a power profile + settings tuned for office work. Mutually exclusive with Gaming Mode - turning one on automatically turns the other off. Turning it off briefly restarts Explorer (a short desktop flicker, expected).",
                ["Help_Opt_GamingMode"] = "Same pattern as Office Mode, reversed - a profile tuned for gaming. Mutually exclusive with Office Mode.",
                ["Help_Opt_Drivers"] = "The circular scan button checks AMD/NVIDIA (official pages), Windows Update, AND the Microsoft Update Catalog (by Hardware ID) in sequence - all merged into ONE list. The action button per result differs: AMD/NVIDIA open the download page (no auto-install), Windows Update installs in the background, Catalog creates an automatic restore point FIRST before installing. If Dell/SDIO is detected, extra buttons appear for their official tool.",
                ["Help_Opt_DriverBackup"] = "\"Backup\" saves all current drivers to a folder you choose (DISM export). \"Restore\" reinstalls them from a backup (pnputil), after confirmation.",
                ["Help_Opt_DriverStore"] = "\"Scan\" groups Driver Store packages by file and flags ONLY the older duplicates of each group as deletable - the newest is always kept. \"Delete\" per row removes that specific duplicate package (pnputil delete-driver).",
                ["Help_Opt_SoftwareUpdate"] = "\"Scan\" runs \"winget upgrade\" for all installed apps. Select rows (or \"Select All\") and press \"Upgrade Selected\". \"Check via Microsoft Store\" complements winget for Store/UWP app updates it might miss.",
                ["Help_Opt_ScheduledMaintenance"] = "The switch creates/removes a REAL weekly Windows Task Scheduler job (not an in-app timer) - maintenance runs even when the app is closed.",
                ["Help_Opt_AutoGamingMode"] = "The switch watches for a fullscreen/game in progress and automatically applies/reverts Gaming Mode accordingly - no manual action needed after enabling it.",
                ["Help_HealthTitle"] = "Health & Maintenance",
                ["Help_HealthDesc"] = "SFC, DISM (Check/RestoreHealth), CHKDSK, SSD ReTrim, broken shortcut repair, WinSxS cleanup, .NET Framework version check. Registry Cleaner (narrow scope - only missing uninstallers/obsolete MuiCache, with an automatic .reg backup). 6-browser Cache Cleanup (Chrome/Edge/Brave/Opera/Vivaldi/Firefox). WinRE health check.",
                ["Help_Health_DiskTrend"] = "A history of S.M.A.R.T. snapshots per drive, recorded automatically whenever you visit the System tab - purely informational, no action here.",
                ["Help_Health_Tools"] = "8 independent tools: SFC (system file check), DISM CheckHealth, DISM RestoreHealth (repairs the component store - asks for confirmation), CHKDSK (disk check - asks for confirmation), SSD ReTrim, Fix Shortcuts (broken .lnk files), WinSxS Cleanup (DISM StartComponentCleanup), and .NET Framework Version Check (info only, no change).",
                ["Help_Health_RegistryCleaner"] = "Deliberately narrow scope - ONLY missing uninstall entries and stale MuiCache, NOT a general registry cleaner. \"Scan\" finds findings, pick the ones you want (checkbox per row) and press \"Delete Selected\" - an automatic backup is made before deletion.",
                ["Help_Health_BrowserCache"] = "One button per detected browser (Chrome/Edge/Brave/Opera/Vivaldi/Firefox) - clicking clears that browser's cache ONLY and shows the space freed.",
                ["Help_Health_WinRE"] = "Shows whether Windows Recovery Environment is enabled (green) or disabled (red). \"Refresh Status\" rechecks. \"Enable WinRE\" re-enables it if disabled, after confirmation.",
                ["Help_Health_BatteryReport"] = "Generates the official Windows battery report (powercfg /batteryreport) and opens it automatically in your browser.",
                ["Help_Health_DiagnosticsZip"] = "Bundles systeminfo, the Event Log, and the app's Action History into ONE .zip file - useful to share when asking for help with a problem.",
                ["Help_NetworkTitle"] = "Network & Security",
                ["Help_NetworkDesc"] = "Windows Defender - Quick Scan. Full Network/Winsock Reset, network info, Wi-Fi restart, routing table. Firewall Rules Management (search+toggle per rule), Firewall Policy Tools (export/import .wfw, reset to defaults), Hosts file editor.",
                ["Help_Net_TrafficPerApp"] = "\"Start\" begins kernel event tracing (ETW) to show which app is using bandwidth RIGHT NOW, refreshed every 1s. Requires Administrator rights (the app already has them) - if another tool is already using the same mechanism, Start will interrupt it. \"Stop\" ends monitoring.",
                ["Help_Net_QuickActionsTitle"] = "Quick Actions",
                ["Help_Net_QuickActions"] = "\"Full Network Reset\" resets the winsock/IP stack. \"Network Info\" shows ipconfig /all. \"Restart Wi-Fi\" restarts the adapters (asks for confirmation - you'll briefly lose connectivity). \"Manage Windows Firewall\" opens the official Control Panel. \"Routing Table\" shows route print.",
                ["Help_Net_Privacy"] = "\"Quick Scan\" starts a Windows Defender scan in the Windows Security app. The Telemetry Blocking button toggles (Block/Unblock) based on the real current state of the hosts file - blocks known Microsoft telemetry endpoints, after confirmation.",
                ["Help_Net_FirewallRules"] = "The search box filters (up to 50 results at once). \"Load Rules\" reads all Firewall rules (can be hundreds). Each rule has its own on/off switch.",
                ["Help_Net_FirewallPolicy"] = "\"Export Policy\" saves all Firewall settings to a .wfw file. \"Import Policy\" restores them from a file, after confirmation. \"Reset to Defaults\" (red) resets the Firewall to Windows factory settings - irreversible, shows a strong warning first.",
                ["Help_Net_QuickDns"] = "One click applies the chosen DNS provider (Cloudflare/Google/Quad9) to EVERY active network adapter - no manual IP entry. \"Reset (DHCP)\" restores automatic DNS from your router.",
                ["Help_Net_HostsEditor"] = "Edit the hosts file directly inside the text box. \"Load\" rereads it from disk. \"Save\" writes your changes (with an automatic backup first), after confirmation. \"Reset to Defaults\" fills the box with Windows' default content (not saved until you press Save). \"Open with Notepad\" opens the real file in Notepad.",
                ["Help_TweaksTitle"] = "Additional Settings",
                ["Help_TweaksDesc"] = "Dozens of registry tweaks with backup/restore, AI & Copilot and Performance sections (HAGS/Battery/USB/PCIe). Device Encryption (opens official Settings). Right-Click Options - built-in (Take Ownership/PowerShell Here) AND a full custom menu item builder. Visual Effects presets (Best Appearance/Performance/Balanced).",
                ["Help_Tweaks_ProfileTitle"] = "Tweak Profile",
                ["Help_Tweaks_Profile"] = "\"Export Profile\" saves the on/off state of ALL tweaks to a .json file. \"Import Profile\" reapplies a saved profile on another (or the same) computer, after confirmation - useful for setting up several machines with the same preferences quickly.",
                ["Help_Tweaks_Rows"] = "Every tweak row (across the Main, AI & Copilot, Performance, and Lighter Windows categories) has an on/off switch that applies the real registry/system change immediately, AND a ★ button that pins it to Home for quick access without switching tabs. The search box at the top filters all 4 lists at once.",
                ["Help_Tweaks_LighterWindows"] = "Same switch+pin pattern as the other tweaks. \"Open Indexing Options\" opens the official Windows window. \"Apply Low Resource Usage Profile\" applies every tweak in this card together with one click, after confirmation.",
                ["Help_Tweaks_Encryption"] = "\"Open Encryption Settings\" opens the official Windows BitLocker/Device Encryption settings page directly - the app itself doesn't change anything here.",
                ["Help_Tweaks_VisualEffects"] = "Three ready-made one-click presets, after confirmation: \"Best Appearance\" (all visual effects on), \"Best Performance\" (all off, lighter UI), \"Balanced\" (Windows decides automatically).",
                ["Help_Tweaks_RightClick"] = "Two switches for built-in right-click options: \"Take Ownership\" and \"Open PowerShell Here\" (they reflect the real current registry state). Below, \"Add New Option\" opens a dialog to create your own custom right-click menu entries (text+command+scope), with a \"Remove\" button per saved entry in the list.",
                ["Help_BloatwareTitle"] = "Apps & Bloat",
                ["Help_BloatwareDesc"] = "Remove/reinstall built-in Windows components (Copilot, Xbox Game Bar, News & Weather, Windows Media Player, Photo Viewer, HEVC codecs). Recommended Apps in 7 grouped categories with real logos (downloaded once, cached locally) - install/remove via winget. Deep Uninstall with optional search for leftover folders.",
                ["Help_Bloat_Builtin"] = "6 fixed entries (Copilot, Xbox Game Bar, News & Weather, Windows Media Player Legacy, Photo Viewer Classic, HEVC codecs) - each with its own \"Install\" and \"Remove\" button, fully reversible.",
                ["Help_Bloat_Recommended"] = "Apps grouped by category (Browsers/Compression/Multimedia/Communication/Tools/Documents/System Libs). The button in each group's header installs EVERY not-yet-installed app in that group together. Each app has its own Install/Uninstall button (via winget) - K-Lite Codec Pack additionally sets a default player. The search box filters by name.",
                ["Help_Bloat_UwpManager"] = "The button opens a separate window dedicated to managing installed UWP/Store apps.",
                ["Help_Bloat_DeepUninstall"] = "\"Refresh List\" reads all installed apps from the uninstall registry and flags the ones that ALSO run at startup. The search box filters by name. The uninstall button per app runs its real uninstall routine, then searches for leftover folders and suggests deleting them (with your own confirmation).",
                ["Help_AdvancedTitle"] = "Advanced Tools",
                ["Help_AdvancedDesc"] = "System Maintenance & Diagnostics (Full Maintenance, Event Logs, Deep Diagnostics, Windows Update repair/reset, Group Policy Editor, etc). Quick-access toolbox for built-in Windows tools + GPU driver restart. Complete, searchable list of ALL optional Windows features. Ghost Device Management.",
                ["Help_Adv_Maintenance"] = "11 independent buttons: Full Maintenance (Temp+SFC+DISM together), Enable System Privileges, Network & Winsock Reset, Clear Event Logs (asks for confirmation), Optimize Memory (GC), Deep Diagnostics Report, Device Manager, Repair Windows Update, System Report, Reset Windows Update Services, Clean Xbox Credentials, and Install Group Policy Editor (for Home editions that lack it).",
                ["Help_Adv_Toolbox"] = "Quick shortcuts to built-in Windows tools: Snipping Tool, Notepad, Calculator, Control Panel, Task Manager, Registry Editor (asks for confirmation - be careful), and GPU Driver Restart (equivalent to Win+Ctrl+Shift+B).",
                ["Help_Adv_OptionalFeatures"] = "\"Refresh List\" reads ALL Windows optional features (DISM) - on failure it shows the real error message, not a generic guess. The blue chips are shortcuts to popular features - clicking one fills the search box automatically. Every feature in the list has its own on/off switch, after confirmation.",
                ["Help_Adv_GhostDevices"] = "\"Scan\" finds devices that are no longer physically connected but are still registered in Device Manager (e.g. an old USB device). \"Remove\" per device permanently deletes it from the system, after confirmation.",
                ["Help_Adv_ScheduledTasks"] = "\"Scan\" shows THIRD-PARTY scheduled tasks (official Windows tasks are excluded). Each task has a switch - turning it off doesn't delete the task, just stops it (safely reversible).",
                ["Help_Adv_BootTimeline"] = "Purely informational - shows total Windows boot time per restart (the same event that feeds Reliability Monitor), so you can see whether boot is slowing down over time. \"Refresh\" rereads the latest data.",
                ["Help_Adv_Autologon"] = "Sets up automatic user sign-in with no password at Windows startup. WARNING (see the red notice on the card itself): the password is stored in PLAIN TEXT in the registry - a limitation of the AutoAdminLogon mechanism itself, unavoidable. Don't use this on a shared or sensitive computer. Fill in username+password and press \"Enable\" or \"Disable\".",
                ["Help_SystemTitle"] = "System",
                ["Help_SystemDesc"] = "Startup Apps (individually toggleable, reversible). System Processes (25 heaviest, with safe termination). Storage - duplicates/large files in your personal folders, always via the Recycle Bin. System Restore Points. Services Optimization (to Manual). Disk Speed Benchmark.",
                ["Help_Sys_MyDevice"] = "Eight informational cards (Motherboard, Drives, OS, Network, CPU, Battery, RAM, GPU) load automatically once when the tab opens - purely informational, no settings here. The \"Export\" button top-right saves ALL of this information to a real PDF file on the Desktop and opens it automatically.",
                ["Help_Sys_Startup"] = "\"Refresh\" rereads the startup apps list, with an estimated delay per app where available. Each app has its own switch - fully reversible.",
                ["Help_Sys_Processes"] = "\"Free Memory\" trims the working set of background apps (does NOT terminate them), after confirmation. \"Refresh\" reloads the process list and records memory samples for the trend history. Every process (except critical system ones) has a \"Terminate\" button, after confirmation.",
                ["Help_Sys_Storage"] = "\"Find Duplicates\"/\"Find Large Files\" scan your personal folders. If OneDrive/Google Drive/Dropbox is detected, extra buttons appear specifically for those sync folders. Each result shows an \"AI-style\" delete-safety estimate (Low/Medium/High, based on file age+type - not real ML). The Recycle Bin button sends the file there (reversible); the red Shred button permanently deletes it with 3 overwrite passes (irreversible, asks for confirmation - not guaranteed on SSD/NVMe due to wear-leveling).",
                ["Help_Sys_RestorePoints"] = "\"Create Point\" makes a new restore point now. \"Refresh\" reloads the list of existing points. \"Protection Settings\" opens the official Windows window. \"Restore\" to a point triggers a real system restore (reboot!) - shows a strong warning before proceeding.",
                ["Help_Sys_Services"] = "\"Refresh\" loads Windows services. Each service has a switch - turning it off sets the startup type to Manual (the service does NOT stop immediately, it just won't auto-start next boot), turning it on restores the original startup type.",
                ["Help_Sys_Benchmark"] = "Pick a drive from the list and press \"Start Test\" for a real write/read speed measurement (MB/s).",
                ["Help_SecondaryTitle"] = "Secondary Windows",
                ["Help_SecondaryDesc"] = "Hidden Features (ViVeTool) - experimental Windows features, automatically downloads the official tool; Appearance Settings - 22 themes (incl. Windows Classic), animated backgrounds, menus, language; Installed App Management; Action History; Version History.",
                ["Help_SafetyTitle"] = "Safety & Risk",
                ["Help_SafetyDesc"] = "No action installs/deletes anything silently without confirmation - the riskier operations (e.g. downloading a driver outside Windows Update, system restore) suggest or require a restore point/explicit confirmation first.",
                ["License_Title"] = "License",
                ["License_Intro"] = "This app is distributed FREE as open-source software, under the MIT License - one of the simplest and most permissive open-source licenses. You are free to use, modify, and redistribute it.\n\nIMPORTANT - DISCLAIMER: The software is provided \"AS IS\", without warranty of any kind. The author bears NO liability for any damage, data loss, or system issues that may result from using the app. Use is entirely at your own risk.",
                ["License_Credit"] = "Some design ideas were inspired by the open-source Windows Maintenance Tool (github.com/ios12checker/Windows-Maintenance-Tool), also under the MIT License.",
                ["License_ThirdPartyTitle"] = "Third-Party Components",
                ["License_ThirdPartyText"] = "This app also includes the following open-source libraries, each under its own license:\n\n• LibreHardwareMonitorLib (github.com/LibreHardwareMonitor/LibreHardwareMonitor) - Mozilla Public License 2.0. Used to read CPU/GPU/disk temperature sensors. Full license text: mozilla.org/MPL/2.0\n\n• PDFsharp (github.com/empira/PDFsharp) - MIT License, © empira Software GmbH. Used to generate PDF report exports.\n\n• .NET / Windows Presentation Foundation runtime - MIT License, © .NET Foundation and contributors.",
                ["License_Gpl3Note"] = "Additionally, for completeness, the full text of the GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0) terms is included below. The app's own code remains licensed under the MIT License above - these GPL-3.0 terms are provided for reference and license-compatibility purposes.",
                ["Vive_Title"] = "Hidden Features (ViVeTool)",
                ["Vive_Header"] = "▷ Hidden/Experimental Windows Features via ViVeTool",
                ["Vive_Warning"] = "WARNING: ViVeTool enables features Microsoft hasn't officially released yet on your build. They may not appear, may need a restart, or rarely cause instability. Use at your own risk. If a feature isn't found on this build (see status per row), try the 'Custom Feature ID' field below if you've found one from a trustworthy source.",
                ["Vive_CustomIdHeader"] = "Custom Feature ID (advanced)",
                ["Vive_EnableId"] = "Enable ID",
